cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Actonomy taxonomy, datasets, or analysis tools, please cite the paper in preferred-citation."
title: "Actonomy: A Taxonomy for Describing and Analyzing Agent Behavior"
abstract: >-
  Actonomy (ACT*ONOMY / Act-onomy) is a taxonomy for describing and analyzing
  agent behavior at runtime. This repository contains the codebook, datasets,
  and automated trajectory analysis tools accompanying How to Interpret
  Agent Behavior by Gao et al., accepted at NeurIPS 2026.
url: "https://github.com/gaojie058/Act-onomy"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gaojie058/Act-onomy"
